WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.900
New signs that the

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.468
US could

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.836
be moving closer

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.338
to giving Ukraine F-16 fighter jets.

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.239
President Zelensky

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:06.840
has been, of course,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.041
pushing for this

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:08.808
and reiterated

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:09.876
at every turn, arguing

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.878
that they need the planes, the jets,

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.213
to defend against Russian missile

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.381
and drone attacks.

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:15.148
Natasha Bertrand

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:16.149
has more details on this

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:17.384
with this new development.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:17.784
Natasha,

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:18.651
it seems that they're not

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.686
maybe not necessarily

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.787
opening the door yet,

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:21.788
but can we say at least

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:22.622
that they're still

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.791
not slamming a shot?

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:25.725
I think that's right, Kate.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.526
And so what we've learned

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:27.627
is that two Ukrainian

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.763
pilots have been in the US

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.498
to train with the Americans

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.133
on flight simulator systems.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.567
Essentially they are learning

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.603
how to fly certain American systems.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.871
They're not actually operating

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.572
on those systems themselves.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.740
On actual planes,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.741
but they are kind of

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:42.909
getting instruction

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:43.943
from the Americans

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.345
about how to become better

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.246
pilots, for example,

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.547
not only on their own systems

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:49.482
but also to see how long

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.216
it would potentially

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:50.617
take them

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.451
to learn

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.386
a system like the F-16 burning,

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:53.987
for example,

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.522
or other kinds of American aircraft.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:56.823
So this is described

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:57.690
by a senior U.S.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.425
military official

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.560
as kind of a familiarization process

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.861
as something that is fairly routine

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.029
between the U.S. and Ukraine.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.497
But it is actually the first time

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.365
that Ukrainian pilots

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.633
have come to the US

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:07.834
for this kind of training.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:08.802
So that could be a kind of

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.470
a harbinger of things to come.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.271
Now, at the same time,

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.205
the secretary of defense,

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.339
Lloyd Austin, is

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.240
in the Middle East today,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.241
and he is commenting

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.010
on the situation in mood.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.312
Of course,
very difficult as we just heard

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.647
Melissa Bell lay out there.

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:21.548
But he is saying that

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.083
even if the Ukrainians

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.384
don't succeed there,

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:24.884
that he does

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.219
not necessarily view

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.321
that as a strategic failure.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.022
Take a listen to what he

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.390
told reporters earlier today.

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:32.425
I would

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.294
not view that as a

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.395
as an operational

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.263
or strategic setback.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.933
I think it's more of a symbolic

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:44.104
value than it is strategic

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.405
and operational value.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:47.807
What I do see on a daily basis is

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.809
the Russians continuing to pour

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.745
in a lot of ill trained

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.247
and ill equipped troops.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.382
And those troops are very quickly

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.485
meaning their demise

00:01:58.718 --> 00:01:59.853
So the question now, Kate, is

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.154
how long are the Ukrainians

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:02.822
going to hold out in dark mode?

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.324
Of course, we have reported here

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:04.791
that the U.S.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:05.658
and some of its allies

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.826
have been urging the Ukrainians

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:07.393
to pull back

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:07.961
because, of course,

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.462
as you heard often say there,

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:09.896
the U.S.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.030
does believe that this is largely

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.599
a symbolic

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.700
city of symbolic value

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.168
rather than strategic value,

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.136
getting them to pull out,

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:16.936
focus elsewhere

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:17.570
that may be

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.037
what the US

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:18.872
believes is for the best

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:19.572
for the Ukrainians

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:20.540
But of course, Zelinsky,

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.741
the president of Ukraine,

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.309
still viewing it as a key city

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.210
where they can wear down

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.545
the Russians, their kids.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:25.879
All right.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.081
Well, Natasha, thank you so much.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:28.481
Joining me now

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:28.982
for more on

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.683
this is CNN military analyst,

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.784
retired Lieutenant General

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:32.285
Mark Hertling.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.586
It's good to see you, General.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:34.354
So this battle,

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:35.155
the battle in Boston,

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.023
the defense secretary Austin

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:39.259
and what Natasha just played for us.

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.560
Defense Secretary Austin

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.328
calling it a sum

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.763
having symbolic value,

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.131
more symbolic value

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.933
than strategic and operational value

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.334
if the Russians take it.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.235
What do you see there?

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.705
I agree with Secretary Austin's

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.240
view, Kate.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.074
It has been.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:55.708
And by the way,

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.177
let's talk about mood

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.044
and how long

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.746
we have been discussing it.

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:00.180
Right.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.015
It's been over seven months

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:02.815
since that city

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:03.750
has been under siege

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.517
by the Russians.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:05.952
And on a weekly basis,

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.787
we have heard different Russians say

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.522
they're about to surround it

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.690
and the Ukrainians

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.925
continue to fight.

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.593
And every day I wake up to a text

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.461
from a friend of mine in Ukraine

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:18.498
that says the mood holds to words.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.000
So they have been very successful.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.936
It will never be a strategic

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.571
or an operational victory

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.772
for either side.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:28.241
It will be a psychological victory.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.643
And it already is for the Ukraine

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:31.945
Ukrainian forces

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:33.947
because they have held it so long

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.114
and have drained

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:35.882
so much

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.016
Russian manpower

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.851
in that cauldron of blood.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.053
I wanted to ask you about that

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:41.454
toll on the Russians first.

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:41.921
I mean,

00:03:41.921 --> 00:03:43.323
we have heard from more analysts

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.224
over and over again.

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.925
It's just the bloody toll

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.594
that this progress

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.095
has taken for the Russians

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:51.030
to get where they are in.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.298
What price

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.367
have they had to pay to pull off

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:55.802
to pull this off if

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.370
if the Ukrainians do retreat?

00:03:58.571 --> 00:03:59.539
Yeah, well, let's talk

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:00.640
numbers first, Kate.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.508
And I'm not a big body count guy.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.010
I learned early in my career

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.511
that's never a good indicator

00:04:05.511 --> 00:04:07.046
of who's winning or who's losing.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.781
But Alexi Dunlop,

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:09.949
who's the head of Ukraine's

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:10.850
National Security

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.152
and Defense Council, said last week

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.387
that Russia was losing

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.321
seven soldiers

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.023
for every one Ukrainian soldier

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:17.457
killed them.

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:18.891
The defense of that city.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.660
That is just unbelievable

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.494
from a military

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:22.862
perspective, perspective.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:23.630
And I think

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:24.931
your reporters,

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.199
both Natasha and others,

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.268
have talked about this

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:29.569
general search guy

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:30.837
who's commander of Ukraine's

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:32.538
ground forces visited

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.673
last Friday

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.241
and talked about the state

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:36.209
of the city's defense

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:37.343
with the military commanders

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.245
and said let's continue to hold

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:40.546
because we can't.

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.115
Today, there were reports

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.016
of Ukrainian

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.817
special operations commanders

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.819
visiting the city and saying, here's

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:47.487
what we need

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.489
to do to continue to push the fight

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.424
and kill even more Russians.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.493
So it is something that's trapped

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.662
Russia in this in this area

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.231
that they can't use other places.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.365
We've been talking

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:00.800
also about the potential

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.969
for offensives in counteroffensive.

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:04.003
I believe Russia

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.271
has been on the offensive

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:06.873
for quite some time now

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.374
and they are losing

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.476
considerable amounts of their forces

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.544
in doing that.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:13.513
And soon we will see Ukraine

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:14.047
one more

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:14.947
and more Western

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:15.782
type of equipment

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.083
gets into their hands.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:18.851
They will start their counterattacks

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.186
and their counter offensives.

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:21.954
But the entire time Ukraine

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:23.222
has been holding

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:25.325
the Russian force in this area

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.759
and preparing to attack

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.161
in other places. Yes.

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.762
So interesting this morning.

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:31.664
Also, Russia says that its air

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:32.665
defenses

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.200
brought down three missiles

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.035
over Belgorod in Russia.

00:05:36.035 --> 00:05:37.070
And The New York Times

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.371
general is reporting

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:39.072
that Ukrainian

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:39.906
special forces

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:42.108
made a rare public acknowledgment

00:05:42.342 --> 00:05:44.544
actually today that they conducted

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:47.146
a cross-border strike in Russia.

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:49.048
Destroying an unmanned observation

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.417
tower is how they describe it in the

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.919
region using a drone strike

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:54.454
that caught my

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:55.655
attention because

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:56.489
I wanted to ask you

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:57.190
what you see

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:57.790
really in

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.559
any Ukrainian strikes happening

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:01.361
within within Russia

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:04.630
and also Ukraine saying as such.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.431
Well, those

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.199
who have not served

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:07.300
in the military, Kate,

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.434
I kind of think this is

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:09.435
like a video game

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.037
that you just find a target,

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:12.905
shoot at it, send drones there

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:14.040
But what is happening

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.376
really is intel collection

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.678
to conduct further strikes.

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:19.812
And when you're seeing

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:22.081
the Ukrainian forces launch drones

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.883
into Russian Oblast,

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.451
like Belgorod, like version

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.286
like even outside of Moscow

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.354
and Saint Petersburg,

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.723
that knock down some of their

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:31.891
their air

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:32.792
defenses

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.394
Russia is now having to take

00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:35.428
air defenses

00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:36.963
and surround those cities,

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:39.465
taking them away from the frontline.

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.501
So it's a matter of material

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:42.969
that's moving back and forth

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:44.303
inside of Russia

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:45.872
to the front line of Donbas

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:47.073
and back again.

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:48.841
So if Ukraine can continue

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:51.010
to threaten inside of Russia

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.311
that require

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:53.246
the Russian generals

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:54.747
to move their equipment back

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:56.516
to defend their forces.

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:58.050
So it is all really

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.986
the continuation of this attempts

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:01.821
at attrition, warfare,

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.256
knocking out as many forces

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:04.023
as you can

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:05.057
and at the same time

00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:07.260
destabilizing the defense

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.127
that Russia

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.695
has been attempting to build on the

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:10.897
on the front lines.

00:07:10.897 --> 00:07:12.532
They can't have it both ways.

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:13.299
So, you know,

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.567
when you're threatening cities

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:15.501
that are 100 miles

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:16.869
away from the front line,

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:17.603
the Russians have to

00:07:17.603 --> 00:07:18.504
do something about it

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:20.540
that they don't want to do,

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.308
protect their citizens, just like

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:22.742
Ukraine has

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:23.709
been protecting their own.

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:25.511
General Hertling, it's

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:26.245
great to see you as always.

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:26.946
Thank you.

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:28.281
Let's speak now to CNN military

00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:28.848
analyst Colonel

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:29.949
Cedric Clayton Layton.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:30.483
Good morning, sir.

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:32.685
Thanks for joining us.

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:34.120
Good morning, Jim.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.688
Good to be with you.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:36.756
This has been a bloody fight

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:37.156
for weeks,

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:38.291
so a lot of tremendous

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:39.091
number of losses

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:39.759
on the Russian side,

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:41.093
but also the Ukrainian side

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:41.794
that there's worry

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:43.262
that this is less about dark

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:45.331
mode itself

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:46.732
than Ukrainian forces

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:47.533
showing they'll fight

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:48.734
for every inch of territory.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:49.802
They don't want to give any ground

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:50.269
anywhere.

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:51.037
And I wonder,

00:07:51.037 --> 00:07:52.338
is this the right use

00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:54.106
in your view, of Ukrainian resources

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:55.475
and manpower

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:59.278
No, I certainly understand

00:07:59.278 --> 00:08:00.079
the desire

00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:01.113
to keep every inch

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:02.515
of Ukrainian territory.

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:03.282
And it's very much

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.417
an emotional argument.

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.552
And kind of like the Alamo in Texas

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:09.121
you know, back in the 19th century.

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.957
But, you know,

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:12.124
there's a reality here

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.392
in the Ukraine

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:16.229
need to save as many of it's

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.631
soldiers as possible.

00:08:18.631 --> 00:08:20.233
This is not the right strategy

00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:22.068
for the situation

00:08:22.068 --> 00:08:24.003
that they find themselves in.

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:24.804
There are times

00:08:24.804 --> 00:08:27.106
we have to do a tactical withdrawal.

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:27.707
So other times

00:08:27.707 --> 00:08:28.140
we have to do

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.442
a strategic withdrawal.

00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:31.110
And this is one of those times

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.578
where it becomes imperative

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:33.012
to save

00:08:33.012 --> 00:08:34.447
as many Ukrainian soldiers

00:08:34.447 --> 00:08:35.615
as possible

00:08:35.615 --> 00:08:38.050
to basically fight another day.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:39.452
And what that means is

00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:41.287
they have to really pull back

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.121
to more defensive

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:44.657
positions, ones that they can hold

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:45.591
so that they can save

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:46.192
as many of their

00:08:46.192 --> 00:08:47.360
own people possible.

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:49.428
What does this mean

00:08:49.428 --> 00:08:50.329
for the next step?

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:51.664
Russia has been attempting

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:52.765
some sort of offensive,

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.934
at least throwing more more men,

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:56.102
more manpower, in the these

00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:57.370
without making much progress.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:59.071
Ukrainians planning

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:00.840
a counter offensive.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:05.044
Does ceding back much at all imperil

00:09:05.344 --> 00:09:07.647
Ukraine plans to counterattack

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:08.581
and try to gain back

00:09:08.581 --> 00:09:10.316
more pieces of Russian

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:13.352
held territory in the east?

00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:14.687
Not I think that's

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:15.955
one of the biggest worries

00:09:15.955 --> 00:09:17.857
that the Ukrainian command has,

00:09:17.857 --> 00:09:19.859
and it's a legitimate concern.

00:09:19.859 --> 00:09:21.594
But if you perform a

00:09:21.594 --> 00:09:22.795
strategic withdrawal

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:24.063
in the right way,

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:26.566
you can actually save

00:09:26.566 --> 00:09:27.900
not only your troops,

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.268
but also your capability.

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:29.702
And this is

00:09:29.702 --> 00:09:30.670
what's important

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.638
is to save as much capability

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:33.739
as possible.

00:09:33.739 --> 00:09:36.309
In order to mount a counteroffensive

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:40.346
And then, for example, mount

00:09:40.346 --> 00:09:41.213
the counteroffensive,

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:41.547
let's say,

00:09:41.547 --> 00:09:43.382
in the south, around Boulder

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:44.784
or some other area

00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:47.086
that they believe is softer.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.354
That's the kind of thing

00:09:48.354 --> 00:09:49.422
that I think

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:49.755
they should

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:51.023
be considering at this point.

